 Source: funcheap/south-bay+funcheap/san-francisco\n\nLots of people volunt
 eer around Thanksgiving and Christmas. But what about Halloween? San Franc
 isco has 16 neighborhood cleanup opportunities on Saturday\, October 31\, 
 2026\, giving you an easy way to do a little good and meet your neighbors 
 before heading out for the night. Through Civic Joy Corps’ volunteer cal
 endar\, you can find neighborhood beautification events across the city. T
 hese volunteer opportunities are super easy: grab supplies\, team up with 
 a friend or get paired with fellow volunteers\, and tackle a few blocks to
 gether. Many cleanups involve about 50 minutes of picking up litter\, alth
 ough the full event times vary. Afterwards\, most locations offer a free c
 offee or meal as a thank-you. But the best perk might be sticking around t
 o chat with fellow volunteers. It’s a chance to meet people who care abo
 ut the neighborhood and start making connections in real life. OUR PICK: C
 ASTRO CLEANUP AT HI TOPS Our favorite is the Castro Cleanup at Hi Tops San
  Francisco\, 2247 Market St. Meet there to grab supplies and form your cre
 w\, then help clean the neighborhood from 10–11 a.m. Afterwards\, hang o
 ut with fellow volunteers and enjoy a $15 food voucher. And take it from u
 s\, the food
LOCATION:s offer a free coffee or meal as a thank-you. But the best perk m
 ight be stickin
